#!bovnar 1.1
# units.bvnr — single source of truth for all 262 physical base units.
#
# HOW THIS WORKS
#   Hand-edited. gen_units.py (at the repo root) regenerates the C unit tables
#   from this file on every build; never edit the generated *.gen.{h,inc}. To
#   add, remove, or change a unit, edit a record below and rebuild.
#
# WHICH CODATA EDITION — CODATA 2022 (published 2024)
#   Almost every .factor here is EXACT: either a definition (the 2019 SI fixes
#   c, h, e, k, N_A and K_cd, so the electronvolt and everything built on those
#   constants is exact), or a convention nobody adjusts (gn = 9.80665 exactly,
#   atm = 101325 Pa exactly, the international foot = 0.3048 m exactly, the
#   thermochemical calorie = 4.184 J exactly). Those need no edition attached
#   and none is implied for them.
#
#   ONE value in this file is a measured quantity with an uncertainty, and it is
#   the atomic mass constant behind Da / u / amu (id 40). It is stated at CODATA
#   2022: 1.66053906892(52)e-27 kg. An edition that is not written down is an
#   edition nobody can check, which is why this paragraph exists rather than a
#   bare number -- and it is what a reader comparing bovnar against UCUM's or
#   UDUNITS' own tables needs, since those state the same unit at OLDER
#   adjustments (UDUNITS still ships the 1986 value) and the difference is real
#   rather than a bug in either.
#
#   Adding another measured constant means naming its edition beside it here.
#
# STABLE IDS (ABI)
#   .id is the value_base_unit_t enum value. Append-only: NEVER renumber or
#   reuse an id — downstream C and the Python bindings are pinned to these
#   integers.
#
#   Native bovnar units are the 10 BLOCK: ids 100000..109999, and they are
#   CONTIGUOUS from 100000 up. Read an id and its leading two digits name the
#   vocabulary it belongs to — 10 native, 20 UCUM, 30 UN/ECE, 40 QUDT, 50
#   QUDT quantity kinds, 60 UDUNITS (all assigned by gen_profiles.py), 90
#   currencies (currencies.bvnr). No two vocabularies share a block, so
#   growing one never shifts another; see the layout note in include/bovnar.h.
#
#   A new physical unit appends at the end of this file with the next free id
#   and needs no change anywhere else: the block bounds and the dense table
#   slots are derived from this file by gen_units.py.
#
# FIELDS (one record per unit)
#   .id       value_base_unit_t enum value (stable; see above)
#   .name     enumerator suffix; the C constant is  bu_<name>
#   .symbol   canonical OUTPUT symbol, real UTF-8 (e.g. "Ω", "°C")
#   .factor   to_si_factor: value of one unit in coherent SI (bare float)
#   .dims     SI dimension exponents as a NAMED struct with zeros omitted, so a
#             dimensionless unit is .dims = {}. Field names: length mass time
#             current temperature amount luminosity
#   .affine   true for offset scales (e.g. °C); else false
#   .offset   affine offset (bare float; 0.0 when .affine is false)
#   .prefix   prefix policy: default | info | german | ratio | none
#   .aliases  every accepted INPUT spelling, real UTF-8 (matched exactly);
#             include the canonical symbol when it is itself parseable
#
# COMPACT PREFIX FORM
#   A prefixed unit may be written with the '~' separator ("k~g") or compactly,
#   without it ("kg"). The compact form is resolved by the same longest-suffix
#   match as any other spelling, so a bare alias always wins over a prefixed
#   reading ("min" is the minute, never milli-inch) and no existing document can
#   change meaning. .compact_exceptions below lists the few compact spellings
#   that must stay a parse error anyway; see the comment on that list.

