  # ── Units the profiles needed and this registry did not have ─────────────
  #
  # Each of the six below was, until it was added, the sole reason a run of
  # codes in UCUM, UDUNITS-2, QUDT and UN/ECE had to be refused as
  # error_unit_profile_unsupported: the publisher defines the unit, the value is
  # exactly stateable, and there was simply no native unit to translate it onto.
  # They are not new physics — they are the ones a cross-vocabulary reader hits.
  {
    # The conventional water column, exactly 9806.65 Pa per metre (the density
    # of water taken as 1000 kg/m³ and g as gn), the same convention that makes
    # the millimetre of mercury exactly 133.322387415 Pa. It takes prefixes, so
    # the two spellings anyone actually writes fall out of it: c~mH2O is the
    # centimetre of water ventilators are set in, and the compact "cmH2O"
    # resolves to the same component.
